(text "OUTPUT ROUTING (bom 7, user rulings 2026-10-07): electromechanical relays, no MEMS (ADGM3144 rejected: +-10 V stand-off vs 48 V phantom, 150 V HBM at the XLR, open-only = cannot ground the muted output). Level select 2/4/6 Vrms is DIGITAL (LEVEL register caps VOLUME; SNR 132.8 / 129.3 / 123.3 dB0 sim) - K1/K2 and the R0 tap string are struck: with the V-stage gone (ruling 2) an analog tap would be a load-dependent divider (-1.7 dB at 600 R) or a switched R_f that moves the 0 V output DC and adds up to +3.1 W held. Build-out 10 R per leg outside the loop (default, revisit)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.000 17.000 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "144574ca-76f7-4975-b438-231bfabb556a"))
(text "K4 = Omron G6K-2F-Y DC3 (2 Form C, single-side stable, 3 V / 33 mA / 100 mW held per channel; DC12 -> DC3 2026-10-10, 12 V is SoM-only): COM = XLR pin, NO = I/V output via 10 R, NC = GND. Coil OFF = XLR grounded and amp disconnected - muted with no power, no FPGA, no pulse; the I/V output sits at 0 V DC (R_off null) so unmute is thump-free. Unmute requires RLY_LINE_MUTE (GPIO) AND FPGA_DONE (J2 A1 VUP_SELECTMAP_DONE, 1.8 V bank 0) AND PG_ALL (wired-AND power-good: every LDO PG + TPS3890, pull-up to V18 on the POWER sheet - bom 17(m)). U602 SN74LVC1G11 at V18 (1.65-5.5 V part) -> U601 ULN2003V12 (1.8 V inputs, flyback COM = V33RLY; one package serves both channels, inputs 3-7 grounded). Coils on V33RLY = U603 TPS7A2033 from the 4.3 V pre-reg, EN = UNMUTE_EN: the coil rail does not exist until DONE AND PG_ALL AND GPIO (second mute path, survives a shorted U601 output) and its 33 mA steps / flyback never touch V33D (bom 7, 17(e))." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.000 24.000 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "95f5959d-f0ff-43ab-8247-daacb862e7cc"))
(text "XLR J601/J602 = Neutrik NC3MD-H-B (LOCKED 2026-10-10: D-size black metal shell, gold, horizontal PCB; footprint bfdac:Neutrik_NC3MD-H from the Neutrik drawing - flange reaches 3 mm below the board, board edge >= 20.2 mm in front of the pin row) Pin 1 = shield, G = shell (both GND here; chassis-vs-signal ground split is a layout/grounding-plan decision - the metal shell bonds to the chassis through the panel screws), 2 = hot (OUT_P), 3 = cold (OUT_M). G6K-2 pin roles (coil 1(+)/8, COM 3/6, NC 2/7, NO 4/5) read from the KiCad Relay:G6K-2 symbol graphics and matched by the user's GN-relay reading; footprint Relay_SMD:Relay_DPDT_Omron_G6K-2F-Y. 70 C ambient limit: place at the rear-panel edge, away from the I/V heat zone." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.000 31.000 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "a11de346-6944-4402-81da-4d0966f2b244"))
(text "L channel" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 30.000 58.000 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "01d2f025-b9c9-4908-a6ab-f0b969705a65"))
